From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 06:30:58 -0400
Subject: mac: the profile lives in Stedding's own folder, and an early one
 comes across

The Mac builds kept the profile in ~/Library/Application Support/Chromium,
Chromium's default for an unbranded build: any Chromium on the same Mac
shares that folder, so two browsers would run in one profile with one
process singleton between them, and passwords would be sealed with the
other's keychain key. docs/INSTALL.md and the FAQ already promised
~/Library/Application Support/Stedding, which is what Windows does
(%LOCALAPPDATA%\Stedding, windows N3).

The default product directory is "Stedding". On the first launch that
finds no folder of Stedding's own, a profile an earlier build left in
Chromium's folder is cloned across (clonefile on APFS, a copy moved in
whole elsewhere), before anything creates the new folder; Chromium's
folder is left as it was. Only a profile Stedding created or used moves:
its GCM category names the product that created it ("com.stedding.macosx",
never rewritten), or it carries Stedding's own preferences. The copied
process-singleton links are dropped.

Why: docs/features/windows.md N8; docs/ARC-ROUND2.md round 10 (found
2026-09-19 while reproducing the full-screen crash).
Removable when: never for the folder name, which is branding; the
migration once no Mac build from before this patch is in use.
